    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0824" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg718"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Earl of Elgin to
                        Governor Sir W. MacGregor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Downing Street</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward, to be laid
                    before your ministers, copy of a note from the United States ambassador at this
                        court,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d588-f1"/> inclosing copy of a letter from Mr.
                    Root which sets out the views of the United States Government as to the
                    conditions on which the rights of American fishermen under the convention of
                    1818 are to be exercised.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Copies of the memorandum of His Majesty’s Government which Mr. Root’s
                        letter discusses were forwarded to you on the 15th February last.<anchor
                            n="b" xml:id="d588-f2"/></item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Mr. Root’s letter is engaging the careful attention of His Majesty’s
                        Government. I will communicate with you again as soon as I am in a position
                        to state the decision to which they have come in the matter.</item>
                </list>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elgin.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
